#
# The Basis toolchain every Verus CI job runs against: ONE place to pin.
# Read by .github/actions/setup-verus (used by verus-gate, verus-verify and
# verus-coverage), which resolves each ref to a commit at run time and records
# the resolved versions on every telemetry datapoint.
#
# Each value is a git ref on the Basis fork: a branch name tracks that
# branch's head on every run (what `main` does below); a full commit sha
# freezes it. Everything else follows from the Verus commit: the binaries
# come from its basis-build release (`basis-<10-char sha>`), the Rust
# toolchain and the pinned z3 from the release's version.json, and
# `verus-reach` is built from the same commit. Keep the vstd pin in
# Cargo.toml equal to the vstd version that Verus commit ships (the action
# warns when they drift).

# BasisResearch/verus
VERUS_REF=main
# BasisResearch/verus-tools-mcp. Not run in CI (the jobs call cargo-verus
# directly); its version is recorded on the telemetry so CI runs group with
# agent sessions on the dashboard.
VERUS_MCP_REF=main
